{"role_segment_id": "CASE_001_SECTION_0001_ROLE_0001", "section_id": "CASE_001_SECTION_0001", "case_id": "CASE_001", "title": "K.S. Puttaswamy v. Union of India", "court": "Supreme Court of India", "year": 2017, "section_type": "FACTS", "rhetorical_role": "ISSUES", "confidence": 0.7, "start_char": 83, "end_char": 154, "text": "The case concerned whether privacy is protected as a fundamental right."}
{"role_segment_id": "CASE_001_SECTION_0002_ROLE_0001", "section_id": "CASE_001_SECTION_0002", "case_id": "CASE_001", "title": "K.S. Puttaswamy v. Union of India", "court": "Supreme Court of India", "year": 2017, "section_type": "ISSUES", "rhetorical_role": "ISSUES", "confidence": 0.7, "start_char": 164, "end_char": 252, "text": "Whether the right to privacy is protected under Article 21 of the Constitution of India."}
{"role_segment_id": "CASE_001_SECTION_0003_ROLE_0001", "section_id": "CASE_001_SECTION_0003", "case_id": "CASE_001", "title": "K.S. Puttaswamy v. Union of India", "court": "Supreme Court of India", "year": 2017, "section_type": "ARGUMENTS", "rhetorical_role": "FACTS", "confidence": 0.7, "start_char": 265, "end_char": 343, "text": "The petitioners argued that privacy is essential to life and personal liberty."}
{"role_segment_id": "CASE_001_SECTION_0004_ROLE_0001", "section_id": "CASE_001_SECTION_0004", "case_id": "CASE_001", "title": "K.S. Puttaswamy v. Union of India", "court": "Supreme Court of India", "year": 2017, "section_type": "REASONING", "rhetorical_role": "REASONING", "confidence": 0.5, "start_char": 356, "end_char": 576, "text": "The Court examined earlier constitutional decisions and expanded the meaning of liberty. The Court followed Maneka Gandhi v. Union of India (1978) 1 SCC 248 and relied upon A.K. Gopalan v. State of Madras AIR 1950 SC 27."}
{"role_segment_id": "CASE_001_SECTION_0005_ROLE_0001", "section_id": "CASE_001_SECTION_0005", "case_id": "CASE_001", "title": "K.S. Puttaswamy v. Union of India", "court": "Supreme Court of India", "year": 2017, "section_type": "DECISION", "rhetorical_role": "HOLDING", "confidence": 0.7, "start_char": 587, "end_char": 676, "text": "The Supreme Court held that the right to privacy is a fundamental right under Article 21."}
{"role_segment_id": "CASE_002_SECTION_0001_ROLE_0001", "section_id": "CASE_002_SECTION_0001", "case_id": "CASE_002", "title": "Maneka Gandhi v. Union of India", "court": "Supreme Court of India", "year": 1978, "section_type": "FACTS", "rhetorical_role": "FACTS", "confidence": 0.7, "start_char": 81, "end_char": 138, "text": "The petitioner challenged the impounding of her passport."}
{"role_segment_id": "CASE_002_SECTION_0002_ROLE_0001", "section_id": "CASE_002_SECTION_0002", "case_id": "CASE_002", "title": "Maneka Gandhi v. Union of India", "court": "Supreme Court of India", "year": 1978, "section_type": "ISSUES", "rhetorical_role": "ISSUES", "confidence": 0.7, "start_char": 148, "end_char": 237, "text": "Whether procedure established by law under Article 21 must be fair, just, and reasonable."}
{"role_segment_id": "CASE_002_SECTION_0003_ROLE_0001", "section_id": "CASE_002_SECTION_0003", "case_id": "CASE_002", "title": "Maneka Gandhi v. Union of India", "court": "Supreme Court of India", "year": 1978, "section_type": "ARGUMENTS", "rhetorical_role": "FACTS", "confidence": 0.7, "start_char": 250, "end_char": 338, "text": "The petitioner argued that personal liberty cannot be restricted by arbitrary procedure."}
{"role_segment_id": "CASE_002_SECTION_0004_ROLE_0001", "section_id": "CASE_002_SECTION_0004", "case_id": "CASE_002", "title": "Maneka Gandhi v. Union of India", "court": "Supreme Court of India", "year": 1978, "section_type": "REASONING", "rhetorical_role": "REASONING", "confidence": 0.5, "start_char": 351, "end_char": 403, "text": "The Court expanded the interpretation of Article 21."}
{"role_segment_id": "CASE_002_SECTION_0005_ROLE_0001", "section_id": "CASE_002_SECTION_0005", "case_id": "CASE_002", "title": "Maneka Gandhi v. Union of India", "court": "Supreme Court of India", "year": 1978, "section_type": "DECISION", "rhetorical_role": "REASONING", "confidence": 0.7, "start_char": 415, "end_char": 505, "text": "The Court held that any law affecting personal liberty must be fair, just, and reasonable."}
{"role_segment_id": "CASE_003_SECTION_0001_ROLE_0001", "section_id": "CASE_003_SECTION_0001", "case_id": "CASE_003", "title": "A.K. Gopalan v. State of Madras", "court": "Supreme Court of India", "year": 1950, "section_type": "FACTS", "rhetorical_role": "FACTS", "confidence": 0.7, "start_char": 81, "end_char": 128, "text": "The petitioner challenged preventive detention."}
{"role_segment_id": "CASE_003_SECTION_0002_ROLE_0001", "section_id": "CASE_003_SECTION_0002", "case_id": "CASE_003", "title": "A.K. Gopalan v. State of Madras", "court": "Supreme Court of India", "year": 1950, "section_type": "ISSUES", "rhetorical_role": "ISSUES", "confidence": 0.7, "start_char": 138, "end_char": 195, "text": "Whether preventive detention violated fundamental rights."}
{"role_segment_id": "CASE_003_SECTION_0003_ROLE_0001", "section_id": "CASE_003_SECTION_0003", "case_id": "CASE_003", "title": "A.K. Gopalan v. State of Madras", "court": "Supreme Court of India", "year": 1950, "section_type": "ARGUMENTS", "rhetorical_role": "FACTS", "confidence": 0.7, "start_char": 208, "end_char": 271, "text": "The petitioner argued that detention affected personal liberty."}
{"role_segment_id": "CASE_003_SECTION_0004_ROLE_0001", "section_id": "CASE_003_SECTION_0004", "case_id": "CASE_003", "title": "A.K. Gopalan v. State of Madras", "court": "Supreme Court of India", "year": 1950, "section_type": "REASONING", "rhetorical_role": "REASONING", "confidence": 0.5, "start_char": 284, "end_char": 326, "text": "The Court interpreted Article 21 narrowly."}
{"role_segment_id": "CASE_003_SECTION_0005_ROLE_0001", "section_id": "CASE_003_SECTION_0005", "case_id": "CASE_003", "title": "A.K. Gopalan v. State of Madras", "court": "Supreme Court of India", "year": 1950, "section_type": "DECISION", "rhetorical_role": "HOLDING", "confidence": 0.7, "start_char": 338, "end_char": 369, "text": "The Court upheld the detention."}
